# L §7.6 item 1, §8.4 (tally 2.1.6, issues #89, #51): fee's day d + 1 day, from a row's 9999-12-31, passes
# 9999-12-31, which load doesn't see: the instance is refused at its key (RUN-LIMIT), and a movement whose day is
# refused refuses the places its legs give on every day, so konto is refused at 9999-06-30 and flows(fee, 9999) is
# refused; other, which only gift touches, stands. tally 2.1.5's refcore refused the model REFCORE-NOT-YET.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 9999-12-31
  start 9999-01-01
  end 9999-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d: date
input amt: money PLN

move fee: transfers
  on d + 1 day
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount amt

move gift: transfers
  on d
  leg cash from landlord to other amount amt

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 9999-01-01
  d = 9999-12-31 "plan"
  amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 9999-01-01 start "plan"
  opening[other] = 1 000.00 PLN at 9999-01-01 start "plan"

ask k: bal(konto, 9999-06-30)
ask o: bal(other, 9999-12-31)
ask f: flows(fee, 9999)
=== expect
f: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
k: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 9999-12-31
o: 1 100.00 PLN
  cut 9999-12-31
